bubblewrap (0.11.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  Historically, bubblewrap was sometimes installed setuid root. This is
  a security risk and has been deprecated upstream. It is unnecessary
  on Debian kernels since Debian 11.

  If bubblewrap has been made setuid root via dpkg-statoverride, please remove
  that setting, and instead leave it unprivileged.
  See file:///usr/share/doc/bubblewrap/README.Debian.gz for more details.

  As a safety mechanism against possible root privilege escalation
  vulnerabiltiies, future versions of bubblewrap will refuse to run if
  it is detected to be setuid root.

 -- Simon McVittie <smcv@debian.org>  Thu, 23 Apr 2026 12:21:47 +0100
